  <h2 id="s1">1. Who may use the Site</h2>
  <p>You must be at least 18 years old and able to form a binding contract to purchase from UDS. If you use the Site on behalf of a business, you represent that you are authorized to bind that business to these Terms, and “you” includes that business.</p>

  <h2 id="s2">2. Business-to-business and consumer sales</h2>
  <p>UDS sells primarily to automotive, truck, fleet, agricultural and industrial trade customers. Wholesale, dealer and “net” pricing is offered only to approved trade accounts and may be withdrawn at any time. Where a purchaser is a consumer under applicable law, nothing in these Terms limits any right that cannot lawfully be limited; every limitation in these Terms applies <i>to the fullest extent permitted by law</i>.</p>

  <h2 id="s3">3. Accounts and security</h2>
  <p>You are responsible for all activity under your account and for keeping your credentials confidential. Notify us immediately of any unauthorized use. We may refuse, suspend or close any account at our discretion, including for suspected fraud, abuse, reselling of confidential pricing, or violation of these Terms.</p>

  <h2 id="s4">4. Orders, acceptance and cancellation</h2>
  <p>Your order is an <b>offer</b> to purchase. Our order confirmation e-mail is an acknowledgement only. A contract is formed only when we <b>ship</b> the goods or, for custom builds, when we begin fabrication. We may refuse or cancel any order, in whole or in part, for any lawful reason, including suspected fraud, pricing or description errors, unavailability, or export restrictions; in that case our sole obligation is to refund any amount you paid for the cancelled portion. Stock orders may be cancelled by you before shipment; custom orders may be cancelled only as set out in Section 9. Unused stock parts may be returned within <b>14 days</b> of delivery with an RMA number, as set out in our <a href="/return-policy">Return, Refund &amp; Warranty Policy</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="s5">5. Pricing, errors and availability</h2>
  <p>All prices are in U.S. dollars, exclude taxes, duties and shipping unless stated, and are subject to change without notice. Our catalog contains thousands of part numbers compiled from multiple sources. <b>Despite our efforts, pricing, stock, images, dimensions, weights and descriptions may contain errors or be out of date.</b> If an item is listed at an incorrect price or with incorrect information, we may cancel the order and refund you, or contact you with the correct information and give you the option to proceed. Stock indications (“in stock,” quantities, “backorder”) are estimates and are not a guarantee of availability. Free-shipping thresholds and promotions apply only as described and may be withdrawn at any time.</p>

  <h2 id="s6">6. Payment</h2>
  <p>Payment is due at the time of order unless we have approved trade credit terms in writing. You represent that you are authorized to use the payment method provided. We may pre-authorize your card and hold funds pending stock verification. Approved trade accounts with terms agree to pay invoices in full by the due date; overdue balances accrue a finance charge of 1.5% per month (18% per year) or the maximum lawful rate, whichever is lower, plus all costs of collection including reasonable attorneys’ fees. We may place any account on hold and withhold shipments while a balance is past due. Returned checks and charge-backs found to be without merit are subject to a $35 fee.</p>
  <p><strong>Saved payment methods.</strong> To process your orders faster, we may securely save your card details with our payment processor, Stripe, when you pay by card while signed in to your account. Cards are saved by default; if you prefer that we do not keep your card, tick “Don’t save my card for future purchases” at checkout. We never see or store your full card number. A saved card may be charged for orders you place or authorize, including orders our team or UDS Assistant places for you after you confirm them, and for the balance of invoices you owe. You can remove a saved card at any time under My Account → Profile &amp; security.</p>

  <h2 id="s7">7. Shipping, title and risk of loss</h2>
  <p>Unless otherwise agreed in writing, all sales are <b>F.O.B. our facility, Florida</b>. Title and risk of loss pass to you when we deliver the goods to the carrier. Shipping dates are estimates only; we are not liable for carrier delays. You must inspect deliveries on receipt and report shortages, damage or incorrect items to us within <b>5 business days</b>; claims not reported within that period are waived to the extent permitted by law. Concealed-damage claims must be filed with the carrier and reported to us within the same period, with photographs of the packaging and goods. You are responsible for all import duties, taxes and brokerage fees on international shipments and for compliance with export laws.</p>
  <p><b>Shipping charges.</b> Shipping is quoted at checkout from live UPS and FedEx rates for the destination and the actual parcels in the order (we do not ship by USPS). We pack to carrier rules: every complete driveshaft, every length of tubing and any single part over 35 lb ships in its own box; other components are combined in boxes of up to 50 lb. Each box carries its own label and is rated separately, so an order that needs several boxes is charged the sum of those rates. Where a live rate cannot be obtained for your address, contact us and we will quote shipping before the order ships. Full details are in our <a href="/shipping-policy">Shipping Policy</a>.</p>
  <p><b>Freight (LTL) shipments.</b> Orders of five or more tubes or complete driveshafts, orders of 100 lb or more, and any single piece longer than 108 inches are packed on a pallet and shipped by LTL truck freight. Freight is quoted at checkout from live carrier rates. Freight rates assume delivery to a business with a loading dock unless you tell us at checkout that the delivery is to a residence or needs a liftgate, so please answer that question accurately. You or your representative must be available to receive a freight delivery and to note any visible damage on the delivery receipt before signing.</p>
  <p><b>Free shipping.</b> We offer free U.S. ground shipping on orders over <b>${{ number_format(config('uds.free_shipping_min')) }}</b>. The offer applies to shipments within the contiguous (lower 48) United States only. <b>Custom cut tubing and complete driveshafts</b> (premade, short couple, unwelded assemblies, vehicle-specific driveshafts and shafts built through the online builder) do not count toward the ${{ number_format(config('uds.free_shipping_min')) }} threshold and are never shipped free: when the rest of the order qualifies, the remaining parts ship free and you pay only the carrier rate for the tube and driveshaft boxes, shown as its own option at checkout. Orders that ship by freight on a pallet never ship free, and free-shipping coupons do not apply to freight. Free shipping is ground service; expedited services, Alaska, Hawaii, U.S. territories, APO/FPO and international destinations are always charged at the quoted rate. We may change or withdraw the offer at any time; the rule in force when your order is placed applies.</p>
  <p><b>International shipments.</b> We ship internationally by UPS Worldwide and DHL Express at the rate quoted at checkout. International orders ship DAP (delivered at place): import duties, taxes, customs brokerage and any fees charged by the destination country are not included in our price and are paid by the recipient. Some long or heavy items cannot be shipped internationally as parcels; contact us for a quote.</p>

  <h2 id="s8">8. Fitment, cross-reference and specifications</h2>
  <p>Our catalog identifies parts by series, dimensions, and by reference to the part numbers of other manufacturers (for example Spicer<sup>®</sup>/Dana<sup>®</sup>, Neapco<sup>®</sup> and vehicle manufacturers). <b>Those names and numbers are used solely to identify compatibility and interchange, and are not a representation that a part is manufactured by, licensed by or affiliated with that manufacturer</b> unless the brand of the part is expressly stated as such. Parts sold under a UDS part number (including numbers ending in “U”) are UDS-brand replacement parts manufactured or sourced by UDS to fit the referenced application.</p>
  <p><b>You are solely responsible for verifying that a part is correct for your application before ordering and before installation</b>, including by measuring your existing components against our published dimensions and measuring guides. Interchange and application data is compiled from manufacturer catalogs, industry sources and our own measurements, is provided for convenience, and may contain errors. UDS does not warrant fitment based on year/make/model, VIN, or a cross-referenced number. Photographs are representative and may not depict the exact item shipped.</p>

  <h2 id="s9">9. Custom-built driveshafts</h2>
  <p>Custom, cut-to-length, balanced, and built-to-order driveshafts (“<b>Custom Builds</b>”) are manufactured to the dimensions, series, yokes and specifications that <b>you</b> supply through our designer tools, forms, phone or e-mail. <b>You are solely responsible for the accuracy of every measurement and specification you provide.</b> UDS builds to your numbers; we do not and cannot verify your vehicle. Once fabrication begins, Custom Builds are <b>non-cancellable and non-returnable</b>, and a build that does not fit because of a measurement or specification you supplied is not a defect. Custom Builds are balanced to industry-standard tolerances for the stated speed range; vibration arising from angles, worn mating components, vehicle modifications, or installation is not a defect. Fabrication lead times are estimates only.</p>

  <h2 id="s10">10. Installation, use and safety</h2>
  <p>Driveline components are safety-critical. Products must be installed, torqued, phased, lubricated and inspected by a qualified technician in accordance with the vehicle manufacturer’s procedures and applicable industry standards. You assume all risk arising from improper installation, use beyond rated torque, speed, angle or load, use in racing, off-road, competition, modified or lifted vehicles, or use in any application for which the product was not designed. Products are not tested or certified for any specific vehicle unless expressly stated. Some products may contain chemicals known to the State of California to cause cancer or reproductive harm; see the Proposition 65 notice on the product or packaging where applicable.</p>

